# A protocol SPEC declared in a NON-MAIN unit, dispatched through a
# protocol-typed field -- the shape zvfs uses.
#
# `protocol_receiver_alias{,_dispatch}.z` cover an aliased receiver
# (`{t: this.view}`, the only way to mark one) on a protocol declared in the
# MAIN unit. There the spec's `this` resolves through `protocolThisContext`
# and the receiver is KEPT as a real parameter, excluded from a call's
# required arguments by the recorded alias name. A protocol in any other unit
# takes the opposite branch: the receiver is DROPPED, and its alias must still
# be recorded, because a bodyless spec has no second chance to say which
# parameter is the receiver. Miss that and every dispatched call is refused
# with "missing required argument 't'".
#
# The receiver reaches this program's dispatch sites through a cross-unit
# constructor, so the vtable wrapper and the vtable function-pointer type are
# both built in the unit that declares the protocol and read in the unit that
# calls it. Every call takes an argument, keeping this fixture about the
# receiver drop; `protocol_facet_zeroarg.z` covers the zero-arg dispatch matrix.
main: function is {
    box: xunit_protoalias.mkBox start: 10
    box.r.bump by: 4
    print "peek=\{box.r.peek scale: 2} tally=\{box.r.tally extra: 100}"
}
